---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
error[returned_local_address]: this returns the address of the local `count`, which is gone once the procedure returns
  --> tests/lint/returned_local_address/bad.jai:9:12
   |
 9 |     return *count;
   |            ^^^^^^
   |            ------ stack storage borrowed here
   |
   = help: return the value itself, take the memory from an allocator (`New`, `alloc`), or have the caller pass the place to fill
   = note: `returned_local_address` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/returned_local_address

